sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch05-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because protozoa, bacteria and other minute cells are of a size at which form is mainly controlled by molecular forces, they exhibit only a limited range of forms, which vary with physical conditions.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Small organisms show a limited range of forms because molecular forces control them";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter V, “The Forms of Cells”; topic “Limited range of forms in small organisms”. Scope: unicellular organisms, bacteria, spores and free cells"
}
